WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.800
Is Zack Snyder's Justice League a hit?&nbsp;
It seems like it, based on the anecdotal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.840
evidence of buzz and conversation around HBO&nbsp;
Max's streaming-exclusive director's cut of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.200
the DC Comics superhero epic. But since streaming&nbsp;
services generally don't release detailed viewer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.280
data — and when they do say how many people&nbsp;
watched something, there's no reliable way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.440
check it. People who want to quantify the success&nbsp;
of a piece of streaming entertainment have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.600
harder time doing it. When trying to measure&nbsp;
the popularity of a streaming movie or show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.920
there are no easy numbers like box-office&nbsp;
grosses for theatrical releases or Nielsen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.720
ratings for broadcast TV shows. The only&nbsp;
ways to try to quantify it require muddled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.360
estimates of ambiguous metrics that don't&nbsp;
provide anything close to a complete picture.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.120
We will probably never know for sure how&nbsp;
many people watched Ben Affleck's Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.960
finally meet Jared Leto's Joker, and&nbsp;
all the hours leading up to that moment.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.920
That being said, the grain-of-salt numbers we do&nbsp;
have should be very exciting for anyone invested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.720
in the success of the Snyder Cut. Bloomberg&nbsp;
reports that downloads of the HBO Max mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:04.880
app increased 64% for the week ending March 28th&nbsp;
over the previous week, according to app data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.800
analysis service Apptopia. 1.48 million people&nbsp;
downloaded the app — though as Forbes notes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.440
that number isn't necessarily "new subscribers,"&nbsp;
as it may include users who already had access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:21.200
to HBO Max, but hadn't yet activated the&nbsp;
mobile app. Bloomberg also reports an 8.9%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.560
increase in users opening the app,&nbsp;
a total of 119.1 million launches.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.360
Those numbers sound big, but&nbsp;
let's put them in context.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.520
They are indeed good numbers — especially&nbsp;
compared to HBO Max's competitors.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.400
For the same week, Bloomberg reports&nbsp;
69.7 million app sessions for Disney+,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.080
an increase of 0.4% from the previous week,&nbsp;
and a 4% increase in mobile app downloads.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.040
Disney's streaming service already has over 100&nbsp;
million subscribers, according to The Verge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:54.720
while HBO Max is projected to have between&nbsp;
67 and 70 million subscribers by the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.520
the year. So HBO Max's app outperformed&nbsp;
Disney+ the same week Disney+ premiered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.920
a new Marvel limited series, The Falcon&nbsp;
and the Winter Soldier. Not too shabby.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.000
No other app showed that kind of user&nbsp;
growth in the week that ended on March 28th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.240
according to Apptopia's data. Netflix&nbsp;
app downloads actually declined by 1%,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.760
though Netflix's market dominance&nbsp;
means that growth will naturally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:21.280
be slower. Netflix has over 200 million&nbsp;
subscribers worldwide, according to CNBC.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.360
There are also positive numbers for people&nbsp;
streaming Zack Snyder's Justice League on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:32.080
other devices, too. SambaTV, another third-party&nbsp;
data analytics app, reports that 2.2 million U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:38.080
households and 954,000 U.K. households watched&nbsp;
the film in its first week of release on,

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.840
"Opted-in SmartTVs with 'automatic&nbsp;
content recognition' technology."

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.160
The limited nature of that data set means&nbsp;
the actual number is likely much higher.&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.040
The viewer numbers for Zack Snyder's Justice&nbsp;
League are below Wonder Woman 1984's first-week&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.120
viewer estimate — over 3 million American&nbsp;
households watched Patty Jenkins' Wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:59.840
Woman sequel on HBO Max in the week between&nbsp;
Christmas and New Year's. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.040
Wonder Woman 1984 is more of a sibling competitor.&nbsp;
The actual threat came from The Falcon and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.360
Winter Soldier, which Zack Snyder's Justice&nbsp;
League appears to have handily overcome.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.680
According to Deadline, SambaTV found&nbsp;
1.8 million households watched at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.320
least five of the movie’s 242 minutes in&nbsp;
the movie's first three days of release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.360
while 1.7 million households watched the Marvel&nbsp;
limited series in the same time frame. Justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.040
League's victory is also pretty impressive&nbsp;
in light of the fact that the Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.400
Endgame sequel series is Disney+'s biggest&nbsp;
series premiere yet, according to Variety,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.320
posting higher first weekend numbers&nbsp;
than WandaVision and The Mandalorian.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.560
Of course, the viewer numbers themselves aren't&nbsp;
the most important metric for streaming services.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.640
The most important things are sign-ups and&nbsp;
subscriber retention. It's a little too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.440
early to say if the $70 million Warner Bros.&nbsp;
put up to finish Zack Snyder's Justice League&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.640
was money well spent, in terms of driving and&nbsp;
retaining HBO Max subscriptions. We may never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.360
know the film's profit and loss. Even thinking&nbsp;
about how to calculate that is complicated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.480
and maybe it doesn't matter. If&nbsp;
the Snyder Cut's true purpose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.800
was to plant positive feelings about HBO&nbsp;
Max in the minds of millions of people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.000
AT&amp;T — the parent company of the WarnerMedia&nbsp;
conglomerate — is probably happy with the result.

